  "_comment": "Platform-curated config that is NOT in the approval workflow: approved models (with pricing metadata), blueprints + options, GitHub export orgs. Skills, typed tools, MCP servers and A2A agents moved to the unified AI Registry (seeded from console/registry-seed.json into console/ai-registry.json).",
  "_models_note": "Vendor model IDs verified in us-west-2 (Oregon) 2026-07-15. Claude runs on the standard Bedrock runtime (BedrockModel). OpenAI GPT-5.6 Terra/Luna AND Google Gemma 4 31B run on the bedrock-mantle endpoint (openai/v1/responses path) \u2014 need OpenAIResponsesModel, NOT BedrockModel. GPT-5.6 Sol NOT added: per AWS docs it is only in us-east-1/us-east-2, so it would fail to run in us-west-2 where our agents live. No Meta/DeepSeek/Mistral/gpt-oss/Chinese-vendor models per platform policy. Gemma 3 removed per request. The acme.triage-ft entry is the ML Platform integration demo (T16/WS-E): an ILLUSTRATIVE fine-tuned model \u2014 its SageMaker training job and Bedrock custom-model import are concept-level (no such model exists in the account); its registry entry, lineage rendering, versioning and consumer derivation in the console are live.",
