  "_blueprints_note": "Predefined Foundation Harness templates the platform publishes. Each is a pre-chosen combination of framework + deploy target + build + protocol + memory + streaming + identity/guardrails, with the foundation (identity/memory/observability/guardrails) pre-wired. Domain teams pick one and add only their domain harness. These are shown as the platform's catalog of ready templates; the console can deploy the Strands/AgentCore-Runtime ones for real (chat + workflow), the rest illustrate common combinations. template.defaultModel must be the id of an approved entry in `models` (null = the blueprint needs no LLM, e.g. a pure tool server); template.tools lists Skill/MCPServer ids from console/registry-seed.json the blueprint pre-wires; template.observability names the pre-wired telemetry. All three are validated at synth by infra/platform-registry/bin/app.ts \u2014 a dangling reference fails the deploy.",
  "_githubOrgs_note": "Mock SSO targets for export. When a domain team hands off to GitHub, they sign in via SSO and pick an org they can access \u2014 the platform's own org or one their domain team owns. `real: true` = the console's gh credential can actually create the repo there (demoed live); the rest are mock orgs shown to convey the concept.",
