    "_compatibility_note": "Framework \u00d7 hosting matrix: compatibility[framework][deployTarget] = reason string means the pairing is NOT supported (reason shown in the wizard); absent = supported. Enforced in the wizard (invalid combos unselectable) and by the registry auto-check on Blueprint versions.",
    "compatibility": {
      "Claude Agent SDK": {
        "AWS Lambda": "Container-based agent loop needs a writable filesystem and long-lived sessions \u2014 Lambda's 15-minute cap and read-only runtime don't fit. Use AgentCore Runtime, ECS Fargate or EKS."
      },
      "LangGraph": {
        "AWS Lambda": "Supervisor graphs are long-running and checkpoint mid-flight \u2014 they exceed Lambda's 15-minute invocation limit. Use a container target."
      }
    }
  },
  "_blueprint_source_note": "source records where the template's actual harness lives. kind=repo: a full exportable repo under blueprints/<templateId> in this repository (AGENTS.md + agentcore.json spec + app code + CDK) \u2014 the compose flow exports exactly these files to the customer's GitHub. kind=github: an external template repository. kind=s3: a platform-uploaded template bundle. kind=illustrative: no published harness \u2014 the entry documents a supported framework/hosting combination only, and the console must say so instead of implying code exists.",
